subtopics.learn:
Memorise the framing: UTF-8 text, `Content-Type: text/event-stream`, fields `event:`, `data:`, `id:`, `retry:`, lines beginning with `:` are comments (use them as heartbeats), and a blank line dispatches the event. Multiple `data:` lines concatenate with `
`; a JSON payload therefore must not contain raw newlines unless you split it deliberately. Know that `id:` sets the client's last-event-ID which is echoed on reconnect, that `retry:` is milliseconds and overrides the browser default (~3s), and that an event with no `event:` field fires `onmessage` while named events need `addEventListener`. Write the encoder by hand once (`f"id: {id}
event: {ev}
data: {json}

"`) so you never mis-terminate a frame.
